---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import FirstViewport from '../components/site-standard/FirstViewport.astro';
import Section from '../components/site-standard/Section.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/site-standard/StatusBadge.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../utils/seo';

const pageTitle = `How CryptoBonusWorld Ranks & Verifies Exchanges`;
const pageDesc = 'How CryptoBonusWorld separates exchange ranking, country availability, evidence freshness and affiliate offer status before information is shown publicly.';

const methodologySchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'CryptoBonusWorld Exchange Ranking & Verification Methodology',
  description: pageDesc,
  url: 'https://cryptobonusworld.com/methodology/',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE_NAME, url: 'https://cryptobonusworld.com' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE_NAME, url: 'https://cryptobonusworld.com' },
  dateModified: '2026-08-10',
};

const pillars = [
  {
    title: 'Official-source-first',
    text: 'Exchange-owned pages, terms and regulator or government sources lead factual verification. Other comparison sites are not authority.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Country-specific truth',
    text: 'A global exchange page, IP location or browser language never proves local availability. Country claims require country-bound evidence.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Freshness is explicit',
    text: 'Evidence keeps checked and review timing. Stale, missing or conflicting facts stay under review rather than being silently reused.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Affiliate separation',
    text: 'A referral link or promo code can be commercially valid without proving ranking position, local eligibility or a bonus claim.',
  },
];
---

<InfoLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDesc} canonical="/methodology/" schema={methodologySchema}>
  <FirstViewport
    family="trust"
    container="standard"
    eyebrow="How we verify"
    title="Ranking, evidence and offers are separate layers."
    lede="CryptoBonusWorld is designed to show useful exchange comparisons without turning a global marketing claim into a country-specific fact."
  >
    <div class="method-meta">
      <StatusBadge label="Official sources first" tone="verified" />
      <StatusBadge label="Country evidence required" tone="review" />
      <StatusBadge label="Affiliate separated" tone="neutral" />
      <span>Updated 10 Aug 2026</span>
    </div>
  </FirstViewport>

  <Section container="wide" spacing="compact" tone="secondary">
    <div class="method-pillars cbw-card-grid cbw-card-grid--2">
      {pillars.map(pillar => (
        <article class="cbw-card">
          <strong>{pillar.title}</strong>
          <p>{pillar.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section container="prose" spacing="standard" tone="primary">
    <div class="cbw-prose">
      <h2>1. Start with the exact claim</h2>
      <p>
        We separate the questions a user is actually trying to answer: whether an exchange exists in our comparison inventory,
        whether it appears available in a specific country, which products or payment rails are supported, and whether a promotion or referral route is currently supported.
        One answer does not automatically authorize the others.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Bind evidence to the country and exchange</h2>
      <p>
        Country context can come from a manual selector or an IP proposal, but that context is presentation only.
        A local availability statement requires evidence for the exact exchange × country pair. When that evidence is missing,
        the interface uses an under-review or unavailable-to-verify state rather than assuming that a global page applies locally.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Keep status vocabulary simple</h2>
      <div class="status-list">
        <div><StatusBadge label="Verified" tone="verified" /><p>Supported by the evidence currently accepted for that exact claim.</p></div>
        <div><StatusBadge label="Available with limits" tone="limited" /><p>Supported, but with material product, payment, account or jurisdiction limitations.</p></div>
        <div><StatusBadge label="Under review" tone="review" /><p>Evidence is incomplete, stale or awaiting a governed review.</p></div>
        <div><StatusBadge label="Blocked" tone="blocked" /><p>A conflict, restriction or missing authority prevents public promotion of the claim.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>4. How ranking works</h2>
      <p>
        The homepage Top 10 is a governed editorial comparison, not a personalized recommendation. The active country is shown prominently,
        but the global Top 10 is not relabelled as a local ranking. A country-specific ranking is published only when the product has enough approved local evidence to support it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Exchange fit, product usefulness, evidence quality, material limitations and current editorial review can inform the comparison.
        Affiliate status does not grant a ranking position and cannot convert an under-review country state into an approved one.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How offer and promo-code checks differ</h2>
      <p>
        We may confirm that a referral route or promo code is present on an exchange-owned surface while still withholding a bonus amount,
        eligibility statement or country claim. The exchange controls final campaign terms, account eligibility and post-sign-up outcomes.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Freshness and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Evidence and commercial records carry their own review timing. Dynamic claims are rechecked more aggressively than stable identity information.
        When evidence becomes stale, changes, or conflicts with another authoritative source, the affected public state is reduced or withheld until revalidated.
        See the <a href="/update-policy/">Update Policy</a> for the operational rules.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Editorial and commercial independence</h2>
      <p>
        CryptoBonusWorld may earn affiliate commissions from approved referral routes. That relationship is disclosed and is deliberately separated from
        country evidence and ranking authority. See the <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> and
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What this methodology does not promise</h2>
      <p>
        It does not guarantee that an exchange will accept a specific user, that a promotion will remain available, that a user will receive a headline reward,
        or that any exchange is appropriate for an individual's financial situation. Current terms on the exchange's official site remain the final source for account-level eligibility.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</InfoLayout>

<style>
  .method-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--cbw-space-2); align-items: center; margin-top: var(--cbw-space-4); color: rgba(255,255,255,.58); font-size: 10px; }
  .method-pillars article { margin: 0; }
  .method-pillars strong { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--cbw-space-2); color: var(--cbw-text-primary); font-size: 13px; }
  .method-pillars p { margin: 0; color: var(--cbw-text-secondary); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .status-list { display: grid; gap: var(--cbw-space-2); margin-block: var(--cbw-space-5); }
  .status-list > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px,auto) minmax(0,1fr); gap: var(--cbw-space-3); align-items: center; padding: var(--cbw-space-3); border: 1px solid var(--cbw-border-standard); border-radius: var(--cbw-radius-control); background: var(--cbw-surface-secondary); }
  .status-list p { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.55; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .status-list > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; } }
</style>
